{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"reveries@example.com","session":"agent:fix-ci-portability","created_at":"2026-10-04T03:10:12.492Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"The required 'Reveries receive-check' check stopped reporting on pull requests and every push produced a zero-job failure for .github/workflows/reveries-receive-check.yml, with the workflow registered under its raw file path instead of its declared name. PR #37 had set a job-level env: BINDING_DIR to ${{ runner.temp }}/reveries-binding, and the runner context does not exist when GitHub loads a workflow, so GitHub rejected the entire file without reporting the bad expression.","decision":"Resolve BINDING_DIR in the step that uses it, where the runner context exists, and publish the resolved path as a step output so the producer step and the artifact upload step still read one directory. Do not put the expression at job level. Add scripts/workflow-loadability.test.mjs, which parses every workflow and rejects run-only contexts (runner, job, steps, strategy, matrix, needs) in load-time fields, and asserts every workflow keeps a parseable top-level name and triggers.","impact":"The required receive-check check reports again, so pull requests can satisfy the main ruleset, and pushes stop producing zero-job failures. Load-time context misuse now fails a local test instead of silently taking a required check offline with no error message.","recurrence_control":"scripts/workflow-loadability.test.mjs runs in test:scripts. Verified by restoring main's workflow: the guard fails and names jobs.receive-check env.BINDING_DIR. actionlint over all workflows reports no findings after the fix.","alternatives":["Drop the binding artifact and post a check run instead","Leave the workflow broken and fix only the post-merge action","Move BINDING_DIR to workflow level with github.workspace"],"sources":[],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
